# Everything that belongs to one race.
#
# Today that is ship INTERIORS - one ASCII floor plan per hull, see
# sbs_utils/GRID_ASCII_FORMAT.md. The folder is named for the RACE, not for the
# interiors, because fleet composition and other per-race configuration are meant to
# join them here rather than stay scattered across the library the way they are now
# (see sbs_utils/SHIP_MOD_PLAN.md s5).
#
# The hull outline in each floor plan is the ENGINE's own is_grid_point_open, captured
# by the LM_TestRange "PROBE hull map" map. Regenerate rather than hand-editing an
# outline; the rooms inside it are yours to move.
provides race_usfp

# Skipped entirely unless 'USFP' is in the PLAYABLE_RACES setting. An interior is
# only ever built for a PLAYER ship, so floor plans for a race nobody can fly would be
# parsed at load and never used.
if settings_race_is_playable("USFP"):
    grid_merge_ascii(media_read_relative_file("cargo_ship.grid"), "race_usfp")
    grid_merge_ascii(media_read_relative_file("luxury_liner.grid"), "race_usfp")
    grid_merge_ascii(media_read_relative_file("science_ship.grid"), "race_usfp")
    grid_merge_ascii(media_read_relative_file("starbase_civil.grid"), "race_usfp")
    grid_merge_ascii(media_read_relative_file("starbase_command.grid"), "race_usfp")
    grid_merge_ascii(media_read_relative_file("starbase_industry.grid"), "race_usfp")
    grid_merge_ascii(media_read_relative_file("starbase_science.grid"), "race_usfp")
    grid_merge_ascii(media_read_relative_file("transport_ship.grid"), "race_usfp")
